{
  "id": "02-the-new-adam",
  "title": "Life in the New Adam",
  "tenet": "Become more like Christ",
  "durationMs": 73440,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/02-the-new-adam.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/02-the-new-adam.json",
  "text": "What if your past no longer gets the final word in your next decision?\n\nA girl had learned to protect herself by winning every argument. When her friend spoke sharply, she gathered the perfect reply and carried it all day. That evening she found the friend sitting alone outside. The reply was still ready. So was a quieter question: What happened? She sat down and asked it. Her friend began to cry. Nothing about the hurt vanished, but the old pattern lost its turn to speak.\n\nAdam's old pattern is familiar: grasp, blame, and hide. Christ, the new Adam, opens another way. He does not erase our personality or ask us to pretend that pain is harmless. He offers mercy that makes truth and love possible together. We cooperate with that grace whenever we pause, repent, listen, and choose as he would choose. We may need to make the choice again tomorrow. That is how a new life is trained, not how God's love is earned. Where do you usually defend yourself before you understand another person? Bring that moment to Jesus. Ask for the courage to tell the truth and the gentleness to hear it. Let your next response carry his likeness.",
